,b)$ will be mapped to the point\n\n$$\n(2a,b).\n$$\n\n- Finally, we shift the result vertically by $2$ units down and obtain the graph of $y=3^{x/2}-2.$ After this transformation, the point $(2a,b)$ will be mapped to the point\n\n$$\n(2a,b-2).\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nSince the point $(a,b)$ lies on the graph of $y=3^{x}$, we have that $3^{a}=b.$\n\nNow consider the graph of $y=3^{x/2}-2.$ Substituting $x=2a$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &=3^{\\frac{2a}{2}}-2 \\\\ &=3^{a}-2 \\\\ &=b-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $(2a,b-2)$ must lie on $y=3^{x/2}-2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["632c6568-7fc9-576e-9071-67a052ce8e78"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "696d1a6c-6fc6-54d4-80b3-eb594b915464" :answer/id #uuid "696d1a6c-6fc6-54d4-80b3-eb594b915464" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-1,-3)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "5683ad40-70e8-5a9e-bb6b-5299bd9ff4cc" :answer/id #uuid "5683ad40-70e8-5a9e-bb6b-5299bd9ff4cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1,-3)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "1932fa4d-0e84-5c29-bc33-ed320d2d5d11" :answer/id #uuid "1932fa4d-0e84-5c29-bc33-ed320d2d5d11" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-1,3)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "3fb2a799-b846-5d20-ba4a-f15e6b349abe" :answer/id #uuid "3fb2a799-b846-5d20-ba4a-f15e6b349abe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1,-8)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "27ef4273-5c13-5f92-82c9-a2b55222a870" :answer/id #uuid "27ef4273-5c13-5f92-82c9-a2b55222a870" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-1,-8)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "23c7f66d-fe13-5a2c-ab7c-e24bba1d00a9" :answer-field/id #uuid "23c7f66d-fe13-5a2c-ab7c-e24bba1d00a9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["696d1a6c-6fc6-54d4-80b3-eb594b915464" "5683ad40-70e8-5a9e-bb6b-5299bd9ff4cc" "1932fa4d-0e84-5c29-bc33-ed320d2d5d11" "3fb2a799-b846-5d20-ba4a-f15e6b349abe" "27ef4273-5c13-5f92-82c9-a2b55222a870"] :answer-field/correct "696d1a6c-6fc6-54d4-80b3-eb594b915464" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "fe3500a7-c6d9-50ea-b641-628c05c03c77" :question/id #uuid "fe3500a7-c6d9-50ea-b641-628c05c03c77" :question/problem "The point $(-1,-2)$ lies on the curve $y=f(x).$ Which of the following points **must** lie on $y=-f(x)-5?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nTo plot $y=-f(x)-5,$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- First, we take the graph $y=f(x).$\n\n- Then, we reflect the graph across the $x$-axis and get the graph of $y=-f(x).$ After this transformation, the point $(-1,-2)$ will be mapped to the point\n\n$$\n(-1,2).\n$$\n\n- Finally, we shift the result vertically by $5$ units down and obtain the graph of $y=-f(x)-5.$ After this transformation, the point $(-1,2)$ will be mapped to the point\n\n$$\n(-1,-3).\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nSince the point $(-1,-2)$ lies on the graph of $y=f(x)$, we have that $f(-1)=-2.$\n\nNow consider the graph of $y=-f(x)-5.$ Substituting $x=-1$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &=-f(-1)-5 \\\\ &=-( -2 )-5 \\\\ &=2-5 \\\\ &=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $(-1,-3)$ must lie on $y=-f(x)-5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["23c7f66d-fe13-5a2c-ab7c-e24bba1d00a9"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "e9b36fe4-7e3c-5256-a2e6-98cdc8053553" :answer/id #uuid "e9b36fe4-7e3c-5256-a2e6-98cdc8053553" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-1,5)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "60e1147e-5dc9-5f98-96b0-207debfc66aa" :answer/id #uuid "60e1147e-5dc9-5f98-96b0-207debfc66aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1,5)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "a79728f8-2e9b-58c9-8dc6-81f0885a0b3e" :answer/id #uuid "a79728f8-2e9b-58c9-8dc6-81f0885a0b3e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-1,-5)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "c534cd05-2086-5e7c-922b-3cc6962ecdd0" :answer/id #uuid "c534cd05-2086-5e7c-9