vertically by $7$ units down and obtain the graph of $y=-f(x)-7.$ After this transformation, the point $(-8,-8)$ will be mapped to the point\n\n$$\n(-8,-15).\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nSince the point $(-8,8)$ lies on the graph of $y=f(x)$, we have that $f(-8)=8.$\n\nNow consider the graph of $y=-f(x)-7.$ Substituting $x=-8$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &=-f(-8)-7 \\\\ &=-( 8 )-7 \\\\ &=-8-7 \\\\ &=-15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $(-8,-15)$ must lie on $y=-f(x)-7.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["abeeca41-84fa-55a4-ba65-c8230425d31b"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "generator" :question-generator/id #uuid "ac44a13f-21ea-5e12-b8ea-59a8bef9ee77" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186059668.py"} [:db/add 17592186059668 :knowledge-point/question-generator "generator"] {:db/id 17592186059668 :knowledge-point/questions ["66562107-64e5-5b2b-99fc-50f565b62c27" "fe3500a7-c6d9-50ea-b641-628c05c03c77" "9a93e41a-bed8-5a57-8ad1-e50ce41e47c6" "3d089253-9314-5487-9a48-4dddc95358e7"]} [:db/ensure 17592186059668 :knowledge-point/validate]]
